_np = [["Read the marketplace's seller rules and fee table before listing anything, and write down the commission percentage, payment fee and any monthly charge in one line.", 'Understand what usually lifts a listing in marketplace search: sales history, review score, price, delivery speed and complete product details; build these strengths first instead of copying competitors.'], ['Compare five product ideas on demand, competition, margin and shipping difficulty; give each 1 to 5 and start with the one that scores highest and is small and light.', 'Order samples from your supplier and check quality yourself, then write the real unit cost including packaging; only products with at least 25 percent margin after fees are worth listing.'], ['Write the title with the main product word first, then size or colour, in under 80 characters, and add at least five photos on a plain background plus one in use.', "Use bullet points for the five features buyers ask about most, state exact measurements and materials, and answer the likely question 'will this fit or work for me?'."], ['Use the formula: selling price minus product cost, marketplace commission, payment fee, packaging, postage and returns allowance equals profit; calculate it for three price points.', 'Set a minimum price at which you still earn 10 percent after all costs, and never go below it in a sale, even when competitors do.'], ['Label every shelf and product with a code, count stock weekly, and set a reorder point equal to daily sales multiplied by supplier lead time plus a few days of buffer.', 'Pick and pack with a checklist: right item, right quantity, undamaged, packed securely, label matched to order; this takes about three minutes per parcel and prevents most errors.'], ['Dispatch within the time promised, usually one working day, upload tracking numbers immediately and send the buyer a short message with expected arrival.', 'Compare three carriers on cost, speed and tracking for a typical 500 gram parcel, and add packaging cost; pick the one that balances price with reliable delivery.'], ['Write a returns policy in four sentences covering time limit, condition, who pays postage and refund timing, and reply to every review within two days, thanking and fixing.', "Record the reason for every return in a log; if three of ten returns say 'smaller than expected', change the listing size details instead of only issuing refunds."], ["Watch four seller metrics weekly: late shipment rate, cancellation rate, complaint rate and review score, and keep each within the marketplace's target.", 'Plan the next ten products by data: take the two best sellers by profit, find similar items, and add them one at a time, checking margin and returns after a month.']]
C['mods'] = [(m[0], m[1], list(m[2])+_np[i], m[3], m[4], m[5]) for i, m in enumerate(C['mods'])]

_dupfix = {1: 'On an 18.00 sale with a 10% commission and 0.50 listing fee, the marketplace keeps 2.30, so the seller starts from 15.70 before shipping and cost.', 3: "Title: 'Kids rain boots, size 28, yellow, non-slip sole, washable'. Photos: front, side, sole, worn by a child, size chart beside a ruler.", 4: 'Price 30.00; product 12.00; fee 4.50; shipping 5.00; packing 0.80; payment 0.90: profit 6.80, which is 23% of the price.', 5: 'Shelves are labelled by letter and number, and a pick list is sorted by shelf. Pick time drops from 6 to 3 minutes per order in a day of 20 orders.', 6: 'A seller promises dispatch in 2 days. Of 50 orders 47 leave on time (94%); the 3 late ones were out-of-stock items, so stock counts are checked every Friday.', 7: "Four reviews say 'colour is darker'. The seller adds a daylight photo and a line about the shade; the next 20 orders bring no colour complaint.", 8: 'Last month: late shipments 3%, cancels 2%, rating 4.5, returns 9%. Returns are the highest, so the seller checks sizing words and adds a measurement table first.'}
C['deep']['mods'] = [(m[0], _dupfix.get(i + 1, m[1]), m[2]) for i, m in enumerate(C['deep']['mods'])]

_dupfix2 = {4: 'A 30.00 pair of boots costs 12.00 to buy. Marketplace commission 4.50, postage 5.00, box 0.80, payment charge 0.90 leave 6.80 profit, about 23% of the price.'}
C['deep']['mods'] = [(m[0], _dupfix2.get(i + 1, m[1]), m[2]) for i, m in enumerate(C['deep']['mods'])]
C['intro_add'] = ["You will read a marketplace's fee table and ranking factors and calculate what each sale really costs before committing stock.", 'You will score product ideas on demand, competition, margin and shipping, then verify a sample, choosing items you can supply and support.', 'You will write a keyword-first title, clear bullets and a strong photo set, so shoppers understand the item and trust the listing.', 'You will compute profit at three price points after commission, payment fee, postage and returns, and set a floor price you never cross.', 'You will label stock, set reorder points and use a pick-and-pack checklist, so the right item reaches the right buyer every time.', 'You will dispatch on time, upload tracking and compare carriers on a typical parcel, making delivery a strength rather than a complaint.', 'You will write a four-sentence returns policy and log return reasons, turning complaints into listing fixes that reduce future refunds.', 'You will watch four seller metrics weekly and expand using profit data, protecting your account standing while the range grows.']
